# ✅ ToonFi Compatibility Checklist  
*How to evaluate if a project is ToonFi-compatible*

---

## Core Question

Does this project feel like a **cartoon world you enter**, not content you consume?

---

## 1. World-First Structure

☐ The site is a place, not a menu  
☐ Visitors explore instead of selecting  
☐ Locations have identity  
☐ The world exists without episodes  
☐ Navigation feels diegetic  

---

## 2. Living Systems

☐ Characters idle or roam  
☐ Environments show behavior  
☐ Objects can change state  
☐ Systems continue over time  
☐ Nothing important is only static  

---

## 3. Episodes as Discoveries

☐ Episodes are found, not listed  
☐ Watching changes context  
☐ The world remains after viewing  
☐ Episodes deepen the world  
☐ Story is not only in video  

---

## 4. Objects over Assets

☐ Collectibles behave like objects  
☐ They unlock, modify, or remember  
☐ They exist inside the world  
☐ They can be encountered by others  
☐ They are not just displayed  

---

## 5. Narrative as Environment

☐ Lore is spatial  
☐ History leaves traces  
☐ The world remembers events  
☐ Visitors build personal continuity  
☐ Story exists outside episodes  

---

## 6. Expansion-Native Design

☐ World can support cartoons  
☐ World can support games  
☐ World can support memes  
☐ World can support tools or toys  
☐ World is not format-locked  

---

## 7. Ownership Philosophy

☐ Non-owners can explore  
☐ Owners gain continuity  
☐ Ownership affects presence  
☐ NFTs behave as world objects  
☐ No core meaning is paywalled  

---

## 8. Phenomena Support

☐ World can host ongoing events  
☐ Systems can change phase  
☐ Outcomes affect the world  
☐ Phenomena leave residue  
☐ The world feels active  

---

## 9. Tone Alignment

☐ Cartoon logic  
☐ Playful or expressive  
☐ Systemic, not corporate  
☐ Curious, not extractive  
☐ Feels like a place  

---

## 10. Final Check

If all episodes were removed, would this still feel like:

☐ a cartoon world  
☐ something to explore  
☐ something alive  

If yes — it is ToonFi-compatible.

---

## Core Definition

ToonFi-compatible projects treat:

• sites as worlds  
• characters as inhabitants  
• collectibles as objects  
• lore as geography  
• and episodes as discoveries.
